   "he": "מִמְּדִינַת הַיָּם. מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה, דְּתַנְיָא, רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: הַבָּא מִמְּדִינַת הַיָּם — לֹא יְגַלֵּחַ, מִפְּנֵי שֶׁיָּצָא שֶׁלֹּא בִּרְשׁוּת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught: One who comes «from a country overseas» on the intermediate days of a Festival is permitted to cut his hair. The Gemara comments: «The mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda, as it is taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Yehuda says: One who comes from a country overseas» on the intermediate days of a Festival «must not shave» or cut his hair, «due to» the fact that «he left» his home «without permission.»"
  }
